                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-3">&ldquo;Paycheck Protection Program Report,&rdquo; US Small Business Administration, August 12, 2020. <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://home.treasury.gov/system/files/136/SBA-Paycheck-Protection-Program-Loan-Report-Round2.pdf" target="_blank">home.treasury.gov/system/files/136/SBA-Paycheck-Protection-Program-Loan-Report-Round2.pdf</a>.
                        <a href="#cf-fn-ret-3" aria-label="Return from footnote 3.">Return to 3</a>
                    </li>
                    <li id="cf-fn-4">For the purposes of these remarks, I&rsquo;m defining community banks as those with less than $10 billion in assets, large and regional banks as those between $10 billion and $750 billion in assets that are not G-SIBs, and G-SIBs as those classified as global systemically important banks by the Financial Stability Board. There are eight G-SIBs in the US, including each of the six US banks with more than $750 billion in total assets. <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.fsb.org/2024/11/2024-list-of-global-systemically-important-banks-g-sibs/" target="_blank">fsb.org/2024/11/2024-list-of-global-systemically-important-banks-g-sibs/</a>
